Consider the following binary search implementation searching for target value 25 in a sorted array of 8 elements. Trace through the algorithm and determine whether it correctly eliminates at least half of the remaining search space in every iteration. If not, identify the specific iteration where the elimination fails and explain why the boundary update is insufficient.

int[] arr = {2, 6, 11, 19, 25, 38, 47, 56};
int target = 25;
int left = 0; int right = 7;
while (left <= right) {
    int mid = (left + right) / 2;
    if (arr[mid] < target)
        left = mid;
    else
        right = mid - 1;
}
